-- title:
--   Both original Gaussian and full compensated negative-mark noises centred at finite-range stopped cash
-- statement:
--   For any finite-range bounded original stopping clock, the actual original stopped full Stieltjes cash plus terminal reward has both the genuine intrinsic Gaussian and the complete compensated negative jump noise as integrable stopped gains, each with zero initial conditional expectation. Jfull includes large negative marks. The source-faithful discounted reward identity holds simultaneously with both centring properties; a direct bridge to the finite-grid signed Ito cash budget.

